    "created_at": "2017-08-16T16:23:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-16T16:23:52Z",
    "body": "@rniwa I'm not sure that I understand the difference between \"protected\" and your suggested \"types only\" mode. The spec mentions for protected mode:\r\n\r\nThe formats and kinds in the drag data store list of items representing dragged data can be enumerated, but the data itself is unavailable and no new data can be added. This sounds a lot like \"you can only read types, and are not allowed to see the contents of the pasteboard\" to me.\r\n\r\nGecko right now doesn't support this mode as we don't have a `protected` mode for our DataTransfer object (https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1199729). We probably should add that and align ourselves better with the spec but don't currently.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
